---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import hiking from '../assets/images/hiking.jpg';

const photos = [{ src: hiking, alt: 'Hiking along a mountain trail' }];
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="A bit more about me — education, interests, and how I got here.">
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>Problem Solver at Heart</h1>

    <p>
      My journey started with high school olympiads, where I first discovered how much 
      I love a hard problem. For me, complex problem solving isn't a chore, it's a joy.
       I like thinking outside the box, finding the angle nobody else tried, and staying with a challenge until it finally clicks.
    </p>

    <h2>Following the Interesting Problems</h2>
    <p>
   I choose my projects based on the challenges they offer and the room they give me to think creatively. Rather than locking myself into one path too early, I want my experiences to shape the career field I end up in.
    Every project teaches me something new about what I enjoy and where I can make the biggest impact.
    </p>
    

    <h2>Nomad DNA</h2>
    <p>
      I have a nomad's spirit: adaptable, curious, and ready to take on any challenge wherever it comes from.
       New places, new people, and new problems don't intimidate me, they energize me. I'm always open to collaborating with like-minded people who want to build something meaningful.
    </p>


     <h2>Why Computer Science? </h2>
     <p>
     Software fascinates me because it turns ideas into something real. With just a laptop and some code, you can solve problems for people anywhere in the world. Computer science combines the things I love most: logical thinking, creativity, and the satisfaction of building something that actually works.

     </p>

     <h2>Let's Build Together </h2>
     <p>
     I'm an active person, and my laptop comes with me wherever I go, so I'm always ready to work on something new. If you have an idea, a project, or just want to talk tech, let's connect on social media and start building together.
     </p>


    {
      photos.length > 1 ? (
        <div class="photo-row">
          {photos.map((photo) => (
            <figure class="photo">
              <Image src={photo.src} alt={photo.alt} width={640} />
              {photo.caption && <figcaption>{photo.caption}</figcaption>}
            </figure>
          ))}
        </div>
      ) : (
        <figure class="photo photo-single">
          <Image src={photos[0].src} alt={photos[0].alt} width={640} />
          {photos[0].caption && <figcaption>{photos[0].caption}</figcaption>}
        </figure>
      )
    }

    <h2>A bit of personality</h2>
    <p>
      coming soon...
    </p>

    <p>
      If any of this resonates (or you just want to talk), reach out — my email's in the
      <a href="/">footer</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .photo-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-4);
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
  }

  .photo img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 240px;
    object-fit: cover;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
  }

  .photo figcaption {
    margin-top: var(--space-1);
  }

  .photo-single {
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
    width: min(320px, 100%);
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  @media (max-width: 48em) {
    .photo-row {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 30em) {
    .photo-row {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
